    "content": "Mogadishu, 18 September 2026 — Liibaan Axmed Xasan, a candidate for the presidency of Galmudug, attended a welcoming and honorific gathering in Mogadishu organized by members of the Cayr community, including politicians and intellectuals. The event also saw the participation of federal parliamentarians from both houses of the Somali Federal Parliament, according to sources.\n\nDuring the gathering, Xasan thanked the Cayr community for their reception and expressed appreciation for their support. He stated that the trust placed in him represents a significant responsibility and serves as motivation for his efforts toward leadership and the development of Galmudug. The candidate did not announce new policy initiatives at the event.\n\nThis meeting is part of a series of engagements by Xasan as he campaigns for the Galmudug presidency. The Cayr community, a major clan constituency in central Somalia, has been actively involved in political processes in the region. The presence of federal lawmakers underscores the intersection of regional and national politics in Somalia.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, this event highlights the ongoing political dynamics in Galmudug and the role of clan-based communities in shaping leadership. Many diaspora members maintain close ties to their home regions and may view such endorsements as indicators of political momentum ahead of the regional election. The outcome could influence diaspora engagement and investment in Galmudug's development.\n\nThe gathering reflects the continued importance of community support in Somali politics, where clan affiliations often play a key role in electoral outcomes. As the race for Galmudug's presidency unfolds, such endorsements will be closely watched by both local and diaspora stakeholders.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/09/18/beesha-cayr-oo-muqdisho-ku-soo-dhaweysay-musharraxa-madaxweynaha-galmudug-liibaan-axmed-xasan/",
